# Agent rules

Read [OWNER-DIRECTIVES.md](OWNER-DIRECTIVES.md) first. It overrides conflicting
roadmap and tooling text. Follow the active `work/WO-*.md`; inspect its allowed
and protected paths before editing. Keep each work order buildable, tested,
verified, and recorded in `STATE.md` and the ledgers.

## Platform and product locks

- Initial support is Apple Silicon macOS 13+. Do not add Linux/Windows code,
  shims, CI jobs, runners, packaging, or portability work.
- Keep platform implementations behind `platform/` interfaces; do not add
  stubs for unsupported operating systems.
- Rust for all first-party code is the active owner-approved migration target.
  MPL-2.0, minimal pinned dependencies, custom-drawn UI, and an owned SVG
  parser/rasterizer remain locked. Legacy C17 code is preserved as migration
  reference; do not resume old C implementation orders. See ADR-0022.
- Never read, fetch, or copy GPL SVG-editor source. Do not fetch external SVG
  resources from the application. Record provenance for external algorithms.

## Repository map

- `app/`: executable composition.
- `src/`: base, platform, XML/SVG, scene, raster, document, UI modules as added.
- `docs/research-r4/`: authoritative operating model and roadmap.
- `docs/research-r3/plan/`: architecture and coding guidance where r4 is silent.
- `docs/adr/`: accepted decisions; `work/`: immutable ready work orders.
- `tests/`: unit, property, fuzz, UI, and oracle tests as introduced.
- `bench/`: corpus metadata, generators, runners, and results.
- `artifacts/`: work-order evidence; `build/` and `.cache/` are generated.

## Commands

The commands below are the preserved legacy C workflow. Rust workspace/build
commands become authoritative only through their implementation orders.

- `./dev build`: configure and build Debug.
- `./dev test-fast`: run local Python tests and validate the ledger.
- `./dev verify`: run the Debug build and fast tests.
- `cmake --preset mac-release && cmake --build --preset mac-release`: Release.
- `python3 scripts/ledger.py validate ledger.jsonl`: validate work history.
- `python3 -m unittest`: run Python harness tests when present.
- `bench`, `fmt`, `lint`, `asan`, and `fuzz` become authoritative only when
  their work orders implement them; do not claim missing commands run.

## Engineering and safety

Use the contracts in `docs/CODING_STANDARD.md`: explicit ownership, pointer+length
slices, checked size arithmetic, bounded user input, no VLAs, and no unsafe
string functions. Preserve unknown SVG/XML source. Keep generated files in
ignored repo-local directories. Do not install system packages or touch sibling
directories. Add dependencies only through an ADR and pinned provenance record.

Never weaken frozen acceptance tests or oracles. Run commands named by the
active work order, then report exact evidence. Do not invent test or performance
results. Keep source files focused and under 800 lines; split cohesive modules
before they grow further.

## Rust migration execution

Follow `docs/product/rust-port-goal-and-plan.md` and ready Rust work orders.
Multiple Luna codex exec processes are authorized, with isolated current-source
worktrees and disjoint modules; coordinator alone changes shared manifests,
locks, interfaces and ledgers. Use Low for inventory/docs, Medium for routine
ports, High for parser/renderer/concurrency/unsafe FFI. Escalate only on a named
problem; use the existing subscription allowance and no purchased credits.
Preserve strict validation, original fixtures/assertions and byte-preserving
round trips. Rust ownership replaces manual C ownership conventions; bounded
inputs, checked arithmetic, safe cleanup and source limits still apply. Keep
unsafe operations behind documented platform/FFI boundaries.
#ifndef VEXEL_SVG_INDEX_H
#define VEXEL_SVG_INDEX_H

#include "base.h"
#include "xml_tokenizer.h"

#include <stdbool.h>
#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>

#define SVG_INDEX_MAX_SOURCE_BYTES (1024U * 1024U * 1024U)
#define SVG_INDEX_MAX_STEP_BYTES (64U * 1024U)
#define SVG_INDEX_MAX_ELEMENTS 1000000U
#define SVG_INDEX_MAX_ATTRIBUTES 1000000U
#define SVG_INDEX_MAX_STORAGE_BYTES (256U * 1024U * 1024U)
#define SVG_INDEX_MAX_DEPTH 256U

typedef struct svg_index_session svg_index_session;

typedef enum svg_index_status {
    SVG_INDEX_OK = 0,
    SVG_INDEX_INVALID,
    SVG_INDEX_LIMIT,
    SVG_INDEX_OOM,
    SVG_INDEX_MALFORMED,
    SVG_INDEX_CANCELED,
    SVG_INDEX_COMPLETE
} svg_index_status;

typedef enum svg_index_support {
    SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED = 0,
    SVG_INDEX_SUPPORTED_RECT,
    SVG_INDEX_SUPPORTED_PATH
} svg_index_support;

typedef struct svg_index_element {
    size_t parent;
    size_t source_offset;
    size_t source_length;
    size_t name_offset;
    size_t name_length;
    size_t depth;
    /* Supported means the element and attribute names fit the current preview subset. */
    svg_index_support support;
    bool closed;
} svg_index_element;

typedef struct svg_index_progress {
    size_t bytes_read;
    size_t source_bytes;
    size_t element_count;
    size_t attribute_count;
    size_t token_count;
    uint64_t generation;
    svg_xml_diagnostic diagnostic;
    bool complete;
    bool canceled;
    bool first_preview_ready;
} svg_index_progress;

svg_index_status svg_index_start(base_bytes source, uint64_t generation,
                                 svg_index_session **out_session);
svg_index_status svg_index_step(svg_index_session *session, size_t byte_budget);
svg_index_progress svg_index_get_progress(const svg_index_session *session);
svg_index_status svg_index_advance_generation(svg_index_session *session,
                                               uint64_t generation);
bool svg_index_preview_generation_is_current(const svg_index_session *session,
                                             uint64_t generation);
void svg_index_cancel(svg_index_session *session);
bool svg_index_element_at(const svg_index_session *session, size_t index,
                          svg_index_element *out_element);
/* Token storage is available only after full validation completes. */
bool svg_index_token_at(const svg_index_session *session, size_t index,
                        svg_xml_token *out_token);
/* On a completed supported child, returns an owned synthetic preview SVG. */
bool svg_index_make_preview_source(const svg_index_session *session,
                                  base_mut_bytes *out_source);
void svg_index_destroy(svg_index_session *session);

#endif
#include "index.h"
#include "xml_reader.h"
#include "platform/platform_task.h"

#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <string.h>

typedef struct open_element { size_t record; size_t name_offset; size_t name_length; } open_element;
typedef struct validation_payload {
    svg_xml_diagnostic diagnostic;
    svg_xml_token *tokens;
    size_t token_count;
    atomic_size_t bytes_read;
    atomic_size_t error_offset;
    atomic_bool failed;
} validation_payload;

struct svg_index_session {
    base_bytes source;
    svg_index_element *elements;
    size_t element_count;
    size_t element_capacity;
    size_t attribute_count;
    size_t root_open_length;
    size_t preview_record;
    size_t depth;
    size_t root_count;
    uint64_t generation;
    svg_xml_reader *reader;
    bool canceled;
    bool complete;
    bool preview;
    bool preview_candidate;
    bool preview_root_supported;
    svg_xml_diagnostic diagnostic;
    svg_xml_diagnostic reader_diagnostic;
    validation_payload validation;
    svg_xml_token *tokens;
    size_t token_count;
    platform_task_queue *validation_queue;
    bool validation_complete;
    bool source_scanned;
    open_element stack[SVG_INDEX_MAX_DEPTH];
};

#define SVG_INDEX_MAX_COMPONENT_BYTES (SVG_INDEX_MAX_STORAGE_BYTES / 2U)
static bool task_is_canceled(void *context)
{
    const platform_task_cancel_token *token = context;
    return atomic_load_explicit(&token->canceled, memory_order_acquire);
}

static void set_error(svg_index_session *s, svg_xml_error code, size_t at)
{
    if (s->diagnostic.category == SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE) {
        s->diagnostic.category = code;
        s->diagnostic.offset = at;
    }
}

static bool validate_document(void *opaque, const platform_task_cancel_token *token,
                              int64_t *out_value)
{
    svg_index_session *s = opaque;
    svg_xml_token_stream *stream = NULL;
    svg_xml_stream_status status = svg_xml_token_stream_start(s->source,
        SVG_INDEX_MAX_COMPONENT_BYTES, task_is_canceled, (void *)token, &stream);
    while (status == SVG_XML_STREAM_OK &&
           !atomic_load_explicit(&token->canceled, memory_order_acquire)) {
        status = svg_xml_token_stream_step(stream, SVG_INDEX_MAX_STEP_BYTES);
        svg_xml_result partial = svg_xml_token_stream_result(stream);
        if (partial.diagnostic.category != SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE) {
            atomic_store_explicit(&s->validation.error_offset,
                partial.diagnostic.offset, memory_order_relaxed);
            atomic_store_explicit(&s->validation.failed, true, memory_order_release);
        }
        atomic_store_explicit(&s->validation.bytes_read,
            svg_xml_token_stream_bytes_read(stream), memory_order_release);
    }
    if (atomic_load_explicit(&token->canceled, memory_order_acquire) ||
        status == SVG_XML_STREAM_CANCELED) {
        svg_xml_token_stream_destroy(stream);
        return false;
    }
    svg_xml_result result = svg_xml_token_stream_result(stream);
    s->validation.diagnostic = result.diagnostic;
    s->validation.token_count = result.token_count;
    if (status == SVG_XML_STREAM_COMPLETE &&
        !svg_xml_token_stream_take(stream, &s->validation.tokens,
                                   &s->validation.token_count)) {
        s->validation.diagnostic = (svg_xml_diagnostic){SVG_XML_ERROR_OUTPUT_EXHAUSTED, 0U};
        status = SVG_XML_STREAM_FAILED;
    }
    *out_value = (int64_t)s->validation.diagnostic.category;
    svg_xml_token_stream_destroy(stream);
    return status == SVG_XML_STREAM_COMPLETE &&
           s->validation.diagnostic.category == SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE;
}

static void harvest_validation(svg_index_session *s)
{
    if (s->validation_complete) return;
    platform_task_result result;
    if (platform_task_poll(s->validation_queue, &result)) {
        s->validation_complete = true;
        s->tokens = s->validation.tokens;
        s->token_count = s->validation.token_count;
        s->validation.tokens = NULL;
        if (s->validation.diagnostic.category != SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE)
            s->diagnostic = s->validation.diagnostic;
        else if (!result.succeeded)
            set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_OUTPUT_EXHAUSTED, 0U);
        else if (s->reader_diagnostic.category != SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE)
            s->diagnostic = s->reader_diagnostic;
    }
}

static bool equal_name(const svg_index_session *s, size_t at, size_t n, const char *text)
{
    size_t length = strlen(text);
    return n == length && memcmp(s->source.ptr + at, text, n) == 0;
}

static bool preview_root_is_svg(const svg_index_session *s)
{
    if (s->element_count == 0U) return false;
    const svg_index_element *root = &s->elements[0];
    return root->depth == 0U && root->name_length == 3U &&
           memcmp(s->source.ptr + root->name_offset, "svg", 3U) == 0;
}

static bool xml_space(uint8_t byte)
{
    return byte == ' ' || byte == '\t' || byte == '\r' || byte == '\n';
}

static bool attr_is(const svg_index_session *s, size_t start, size_t length,
                    const char *name)
{
    size_t name_length = strlen(name);
    return length == name_length && memcmp(s->source.ptr + start, name, length) == 0;
}

static bool preview_attributes_supported(const svg_index_session *s,
                                         const svg_xml_reader_tag *tag,
                                         svg_index_support shape)
{
    if (tag->source.length > SVG_INDEX_MAX_STEP_BYTES) return false;
    size_t end = tag->source.offset + tag->source.length;
    size_t at = tag->name.offset + tag->name.length;
    bool width = false, height = false, data = false;
    while (at < end) {
        while (at < end && xml_space(s->source.ptr[at])) ++at;
        if (at >= end || s->source.ptr[at] == '>' || s->source.ptr[at] == '/') break;
        size_t name = at;
        while (at < end && !xml_space(s->source.ptr[at]) &&
               s->source.ptr[at] != '=' && s->source.ptr[at] != '/' &&
               s->source.ptr[at] != '>') ++at;
        size_t name_length = at - name;
        if (name_length == 0U || memchr(s->source.ptr + name, ':', name_length) != NULL)
            return false;
        while (at < end && xml_space(s->source.ptr[at])) ++at;
        if (at >= end || s->source.ptr[at++] != '=') return false;
        while (at < end && xml_space(s->source.ptr[at])) ++at;
        if (at >= end || (s->source.ptr[at] != '\'' && s->source.ptr[at] != '"')) return false;
        uint8_t quote = s->source.ptr[at++];
        size_t value = at;
        while (at < end && s->source.ptr[at] != quote) ++at;
        if (at >= end) return false;
        size_t value_length = at - value;
        bool accepted = false;
        if (shape == SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED) {
            accepted = attr_is(s, name, name_length, "xmlns") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "version") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "width") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "height") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "viewBox");
            if (attr_is(s, name, name_length, "width")) width = true;
            if (attr_is(s, name, name_length, "height")) height = true;
            if (attr_is(s, name, name_length, "xmlns") &&
                (value_length != 26U || memcmp(s->source.ptr + value,
                    "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", 26U) != 0)) return false;
        } else if (shape == SVG_INDEX_SUPPORTED_RECT) {
            accepted = attr_is(s, name, name_length, "fill") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "fill-rule") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "x") || attr_is(s, name, name_length, "y") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "width") || attr_is(s, name, name_length, "height");
            if (attr_is(s, name, name_length, "width")) width = true;
            if (attr_is(s, name, name_length, "height")) height = true;
        } else {
            accepted = attr_is(s, name, name_length, "fill") ||
                attr_is(s, name, name_length, "fill-rule") || attr_is(s, name, name_length, "d");
            if (attr_is(s, name, name_length, "d")) data = true;
        }
        if (!accepted) return false;
        at++;
    }
    return shape == SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED ? width && height :
        shape == SVG_INDEX_SUPPORTED_RECT ? width && height : data;
}

static bool reserve_element(svg_index_session *s)
{
    if (s->element_count >= SVG_INDEX_MAX_ELEMENTS) return false;
    if (s->element_count < s->element_capacity) return true;
    size_t cap = s->element_capacity == 0 ? 256U : s->element_capacity * 2U;
    if (cap > SVG_INDEX_MAX_ELEMENTS) cap = SVG_INDEX_MAX_ELEMENTS;
    if (cap > SVG_INDEX_MAX_COMPONENT_BYTES / sizeof(*s->elements)) return false;
    void *next = realloc(s->elements, cap * sizeof(*s->elements));
    if (next == NULL) return false;
    s->elements = next;
    s->element_capacity = cap;
    return true;
}

static void finish_open_tag(svg_index_session *s, const svg_xml_reader_tag *tag)
{
    bool closing = tag->kind == SVG_XML_TOKEN_END_ELEMENT;
    bool self_closing = tag->kind == SVG_XML_TOKEN_EMPTY_ELEMENT;
    if (tag->attribute_count > SVG_INDEX_MAX_ATTRIBUTES - s->attribute_count) {
        set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_ATTRIBUTE_LIMIT, tag->source.offset);
        return;
    }
    s->attribute_count += tag->attribute_count;
    if (closing) {
        if (s->depth == 0) { set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_MISMATCHED_TAG, tag->source.offset); return; }
        open_element top = s->stack[s->depth - 1U];
        if (top.name_length != tag->name.length ||
            memcmp(s->source.ptr + top.name_offset, s->source.ptr + tag->name.offset,
                   tag->name.length) != 0) {
            set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_MISMATCHED_TAG, tag->source.offset); return;
        }
        --s->depth;
        s->elements[top.record].source_length = tag->source.offset + tag->source.length -
                                                s->elements[top.record].source_offset;
        s->elements[top.record].closed = true;
        if (!s->preview_candidate && !s->preview && s->depth == 1U && s->preview_root_supported &&
            s->elements[top.record].support != SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED)
            { s->preview_candidate = true; s->preview_record = top.record; }
        return;
    }
    if (tag->name.length == 0U || tag->name.length == 4096U) {
        set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_INVALID_NAME, tag->name.offset);
        return;
    }
    if (s->depth >= SVG_INDEX_MAX_DEPTH) { set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_DEPTH_LIMIT, tag->source.offset); return; }
    if (s->depth == 0 && ++s->root_count > 1U) {
        set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_MULTIPLE_ROOTS, tag->source.offset); return;
    }
    if (!reserve_element(s)) { set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_NODE_LIMIT, tag->source.offset); return; }
    size_t i = s->element_count++;
    svg_index_element *e = &s->elements[i];
    e->parent = s->depth == 0 ? SIZE_MAX : s->stack[s->depth - 1U].record;
    e->source_offset = tag->source.offset;
    e->source_length = tag->source.length;
    e->name_offset = tag->name.offset;
    e->name_length = tag->name.length;
    e->depth = s->depth;
    e->support = equal_name(s, e->name_offset, e->name_length, "rect") ? SVG_INDEX_SUPPORTED_RECT :
                 equal_name(s, e->name_offset, e->name_length, "path") ? SVG_INDEX_SUPPORTED_PATH : SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED;
    e->closed = self_closing;
    if (s->depth == 0U) {
        s->root_open_length = tag->source.length;
        s->preview_root_supported = preview_root_is_svg(s) &&
            preview_attributes_supported(s, tag, SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED);
    }
    if (s->depth == 1U && e->support != SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED &&
        !preview_attributes_supported(s, tag, e->support))
        e->support = SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED;
    if (!s->preview_candidate && !s->preview && s->depth == 1U && s->preview_root_supported && self_closing &&
        e->support != SVG_INDEX_UNSUPPORTED) {
        s->preview_candidate = true; s->preview_record = i;
    }
    if (!self_closing) {
        s->stack[s->depth].record = i;
        s->stack[s->depth].name_offset = tag->name.offset;
        s->stack[s->depth].name_length = tag->name.length;
        ++s->depth;
    }
}

static bool index_reader_tag(void *context, const svg_xml_reader_tag *tag)
{
    finish_open_tag(context, tag);
    return true;
}

static void publish_validated_preview(svg_index_session *s)
{
    if (!s->preview_candidate || s->preview) return;
    const svg_index_element *shape = &s->elements[s->preview_record];
    size_t span_end = shape->source_offset + shape->source_length;
    bool failed = atomic_load_explicit(&s->validation.failed, memory_order_acquire);
    size_t validated_end = failed ?
        atomic_load_explicit(&s->validation.error_offset, memory_order_relaxed) :
        atomic_load_explicit(&s->validation.bytes_read, memory_order_acquire);
    if (validated_end >= span_end)
        s->preview = true;
}

svg_index_status svg_index_start(base_bytes source, uint64_t generation,
                                 svg_index_session **out_session)
{
    if (out_session == NULL) return SVG_INDEX_INVALID;
    *out_session = NULL;
    if (source.len > SVG_INDEX_MAX_SOURCE_BYTES) return SVG_INDEX_LIMIT;
    if (!base_bytes_valid(source)) return SVG_INDEX_INVALID;
    svg_index_session *s = calloc(1, sizeof(*s));
    if (s == NULL) return SVG_INDEX_OOM;
    s->source = source;
    atomic_init(&s->validation.bytes_read, 0U);
    atomic_init(&s->validation.error_offset, 0U);
    atomic_init(&s->validation.failed, false);
    s->generation = generation;
    svg_xml_reader_status reader_status = svg_xml_reader_start(source, &s->reader);
    if (reader_status != SVG_XML_READER_OK) {
        free(s);
        return reader_status == SVG_XML_READER_LIMIT ? SVG_INDEX_LIMIT : SVG_INDEX_OOM;
    }
    platform_task_config config = {1U, 1U, NULL, NULL, NULL};
    if (platform_task_queue_create(&config, &s->validation_queue) != PLATFORM_TASK_OK ||
        platform_task_submit(s->validation_queue, 1U, 1U, validate_document, s) != PLATFORM_TASK_OK) {
        if (s->validation_queue != NULL) {
            platform_task_shutdown(s->validation_queue);
            platform_task_destroy(s->validation_queue);
        }
        svg_xml_reader_destroy(s->reader);
        free(s);
        return SVG_INDEX_OOM;
    }
    *out_session = s;
    return SVG_INDEX_OK;
}

svg_index_status svg_index_step(svg_index_session *s, size_t byte_budget)
{
    if (s == NULL || byte_budget == 0) return SVG_INDEX_INVALID;
    if (s->canceled) return SVG_INDEX_CANCELED;
    if (s->complete) return SVG_INDEX_COMPLETE;
    harvest_validation(s);
    publish_validated_preview(s);
    if (s->diagnostic.category != SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE)
        return s->validation_complete ? SVG_INDEX_MALFORMED : SVG_INDEX_OK;
    if (s->preview_candidate && !s->preview) return SVG_INDEX_OK;
    svg_xml_reader_status reader_status = svg_xml_reader_step(s->reader, byte_budget,
                                                               index_reader_tag, s);
    svg_xml_reader_progress reader_progress = svg_xml_reader_get_progress(s->reader);
    if (reader_progress.diagnostic.category != SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE)
        s->reader_diagnostic = reader_progress.diagnostic;
    if (reader_status == SVG_XML_READER_MALFORMED) {
        harvest_validation(s);
        publish_validated_preview(s);
        if (!s->validation_complete) return SVG_INDEX_OK;
        if (s->diagnostic.category == SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE)
            s->diagnostic = s->reader_diagnostic;
        return SVG_INDEX_MALFORMED;
    }
    if (reader_status == SVG_XML_READER_COMPLETE) {
        if (s->depth != 0U || s->root_count != 1U)
            set_error(s, SVG_XML_ERROR_INCOMPLETE_DOCUMENT, s->source.len);
        else s->source_scanned = true;
    }
    harvest_validation(s);
    publish_validated_preview(s);
    if (s->diagnostic.category != SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE)
        return s->validation_complete ? SVG_INDEX_MALFORMED : SVG_INDEX_OK;
    if (s->source_scanned && s->validation_complete) s->complete = true;
    return s->diagnostic.category == SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE ?
           (s->complete ? SVG_INDEX_COMPLETE : SVG_INDEX_OK) : SVG_INDEX_MALFORMED;
}

svg_index_progress svg_index_get_progress(const svg_index_session *s)
{
    svg_index_progress p = {0};
    if (s == NULL) return p;
    p.bytes_read = svg_xml_reader_get_progress(s->reader).bytes_read;
    p.source_bytes = s->source.len;
    p.element_count = s->element_count; p.attribute_count = s->attribute_count;
    p.token_count = s->token_count;
    p.generation = s->generation; p.diagnostic = s->diagnostic;
    p.complete = s->complete; p.canceled = s->canceled; p.first_preview_ready = s->preview;
    return p;
}

svg_index_status svg_index_advance_generation(svg_index_session *s, uint64_t generation)
{
    if (s == NULL || generation <= s->generation) return SVG_INDEX_INVALID;
    s->generation = generation; s->preview = false; s->preview_candidate = false;
    return SVG_INDEX_OK;
}

bool svg_index_preview_generation_is_current(const svg_index_session *s,
                                             uint64_t generation)
{
    return s != NULL && !s->canceled && s->preview && generation == s->generation;
}

void svg_index_cancel(svg_index_session *s)
{
    if (s == NULL) return;
    s->canceled = true;
    (void)platform_task_cancel(s->validation_queue, 1U);
}

bool svg_index_element_at(const svg_index_session *s, size_t index, svg_index_element *out)
{
    if (s == NULL || out == NULL || index >= s->element_count) return false;
    *out = s->elements[index]; return true;
}

bool svg_index_token_at(const svg_index_session *s, size_t index, svg_xml_token *out)
{
    if (s == NULL || out == NULL || !s->complete || index >= s->token_count) return false;
    *out = s->tokens[index];
    return true;
}

bool svg_index_make_preview_source(const svg_index_session *s, base_mut_bytes *out)
{
    if (out == NULL) return false;
    *out = (base_mut_bytes){NULL, 0U};
    if (s == NULL || !s->preview || s->root_open_length == 0U ||
        s->preview_record >= s->element_count) return false;
    const svg_index_element *root = &s->elements[0];
    const svg_index_element *shape = &s->elements[s->preview_record];
    if (root->name_length != 3U || memcmp(s->source.ptr + root->name_offset, "svg", 3U) != 0 ||
        shape->source_length == 0U) return false;
    size_t total = 0U;
    if (!base_size_add(s->root_open_length, shape->source_length, &total) ||
        !base_size_add(total, 6U, &total) || total > 16U * 1024U * 1024U) return false;
    uint8_t *memory = malloc(total);
    if (memory == NULL) return false;
    memcpy(memory, s->source.ptr + root->source_offset, s->root_open_length);
    memcpy(memory + s->root_open_length, s->source.ptr + shape->source_offset,
           shape->source_length);
    memcpy(memory + total - 6U, "</svg>", 6U);
    *out = (base_mut_bytes){memory, total};
    return true;
}

void svg_index_destroy(svg_index_session *s)
{
    if (s == NULL) return;
    platform_task_shutdown(s->validation_queue);
    platform_task_destroy(s->validation_queue);
    svg_xml_reader_destroy(s->reader);
    free(s->tokens); free(s->validation.tokens); free(s->elements); free(s);
}

#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
//! Bounded progressive SVG indexing with independent background XML validation.

use std::mem::size_of;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicBool, AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, MutexGuard};

use vexel_platform_tasks::{QueueConfig, TaskCallback, TaskOutput, TaskQueue};
use vexel_xml::{
    ReaderStatus, ReaderTag, TagKind, XmlDiagnostic, XmlError,
    XmlReader, XmlToken, XmlTokenStream, XmlSpan, StreamStatus, MAX_LARGE_INPUT_BYTES,
    MAX_READER_STEP_BYTES, MAX_TOKEN_NAME_BYTES,
};

pub const MAX_SOURCE_BYTES: usize = 1024 * 1024 * 1024;
pub const MAX_STEP_BYTES: usize = 64 * 1024;
pub const MAX_ELEMENTS: usize = 1_000_000;
pub const MAX_ATTRIBUTES: usize = 1_000_000;
pub const MAX_STORAGE_BYTES: usize = 256 * 1024 * 1024;
pub const MAX_COMPONENT_BYTES: usize = MAX_STORAGE_BYTES / 2;
pub const MAX_DEPTH: usize = 256;
pub const MAX_PREVIEW_SOURCE_BYTES: usize = 16 * 1024 * 1024;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum IndexStatus { Ok, Invalid, Limit, OutOfMemory, Malformed, Canceled, Complete }

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ElementSupport { Unsupported, Rect, Path }

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct IndexElement {
    pub parent: usize,
    pub source_offset: usize,
    pub source_length: usize,
    pub name_offset: usize,
    pub name_length: usize,
    pub depth: usize,
    pub support: ElementSupport,
    pub closed: bool,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct IndexProgress {
    pub bytes_read: usize,
    pub source_bytes: usize,
    pub element_count: usize,
    pub attribute_count: usize,
    pub token_count: usize,
    pub generation: u64,
    pub diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic,
    pub complete: bool,
    pub canceled: bool,
    pub first_preview_ready: bool,
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
struct OpenElement { record: usize, name: XmlSpan }

struct ValidationResult { diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic, tokens: Vec<XmlToken> }

struct WorkerState {
    frontier: AtomicUsize,
    failed: AtomicBool,
    error_offset: AtomicUsize,
    result: Mutex<Option<ValidationResult>>,
}

impl WorkerState {
    fn new() -> Self {
        Self { frontier: AtomicUsize::new(0), failed: AtomicBool::new(false),
            error_offset: AtomicUsize::new(0), result: Mutex::new(None) }
    }
}

/// A session borrows the caller's immutable source Arc. The validator owns an
/// Arc clone, while the resumable lexical reader borrows the original bytes.
pub struct IndexSession<'a> {
    source_owner: &'a Arc<Vec<u8>>,
    reader: XmlReader<'a>,
    queue: TaskQueue,
    worker: Arc<WorkerState>,
    elements: Vec<IndexElement>,
    element_storage: usize,
    attribute_count: usize,
    depth: usize,
    stack: [OpenElement; MAX_DEPTH],
    root_count: usize,
    root_open_length: usize,
    preview_record: usize,
    generation: u64,
    canceled: bool,
    complete: bool,
    preview: bool,
    preview_candidate: bool,
    preview_root_supported: bool,
    diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic,
    index_diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic,
    validation_diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic,
    reader_diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic,
    tokens: Vec<XmlToken>,
    token_count: usize,
    validation_complete: bool,
    source_scanned: bool,
}

impl<'a> IndexSession<'a> {
    pub fn start(source: &'a Arc<Vec<u8>>, generation: u64) -> Result<Self, IndexStatus> {
        let bytes = source.as_slice();
        if bytes.len() > MAX_SOURCE_BYTES || bytes.len() > MAX_LARGE_INPUT_BYTES {
            return Err(IndexStatus::Limit);
        }
        let reader = XmlReader::new(bytes).map_err(|status| match status {
            ReaderStatus::Limit => IndexStatus::Limit,
            _ => IndexStatus::Invalid,
        })?;
        let queue = TaskQueue::new(QueueConfig { capacity: 1, workers: 1 })
            .map_err(|_| IndexStatus::OutOfMemory)?;
        let worker = Arc::new(WorkerState::new());
        let worker_context = Arc::clone(&worker);
        let worker_source = Arc::clone(source);
        let callback = TaskCallback::new((worker_context, worker_source), |context, token| {
            validate_document(context, token)
        });
        queue.submit(1, 1, callback).map_err(|_| IndexStatus::OutOfMemory)?;
        Ok(Self {
            source_owner: source, reader, queue, worker, elements: Vec::new(),
            element_storage: size_of::<[OpenElement; MAX_DEPTH]>(),
            attribute_count: 0, depth: 0,
            stack: [OpenElement { record: 0, name: XmlSpan { offset: 0, length: 0 } }; MAX_DEPTH],
            root_count: 0, root_open_length: 0, preview_record: 0, generation,
            canceled: false, complete: false, preview: false, preview_candidate: false,
            preview_root_supported: false, diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic::default(),
            index_diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic::default(), validation_diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic::default(),
            reader_diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic::default(), tokens: Vec::new(), token_count: 0,
            validation_complete: false, source_scanned: false,
        })
    }

    pub fn step(&mut self, byte_budget: usize) -> IndexStatus {
        if byte_budget == 0 { return IndexStatus::Invalid; }
        if self.canceled { return IndexStatus::Canceled; }
        if self.complete { return IndexStatus::Complete; }
        self.harvest_validation();
        self.publish_validated_preview();
        if self.validation_complete && self.validation_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None
            && self.reader.progress().bytes_read >= self.validation_diagnostic.offset {
            self.diagnostic = self.validation_diagnostic;
            return IndexStatus::Malformed;
        }
        if self.index_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None && self.validation_complete {
            self.diagnostic = if self.validation_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                self.validation_diagnostic
            } else { self.index_diagnostic };
            return IndexStatus::Malformed;
        }
        if self.preview_candidate && !self.preview && self.validation_diagnostic.category == XmlError::None {
            return IndexStatus::Ok;
        }
        let source = self.source_owner.as_slice();
        let mut elements = &mut self.elements;
        let mut element_storage = &mut self.element_storage;
        let mut attribute_count = &mut self.attribute_count;
        let mut depth = &mut self.depth;
        let mut stack = &mut self.stack;
        let mut root_count = &mut self.root_count;
        let mut root_open_length = &mut self.root_open_length;
        let mut preview_record = &mut self.preview_record;
        let mut preview_candidate = &mut self.preview_candidate;
        let mut preview_root_supported = &mut self.preview_root_supported;
        let mut diagnostic = &mut self.index_diagnostic;
        let preview = self.preview;
        let reader_status = self.reader.step(byte_budget.min(MAX_STEP_BYTES), |tag| {
            index_tag(source, tag, &mut elements, &mut element_storage, &mut attribute_count,
                &mut depth, &mut stack, &mut root_count, &mut root_open_length,
                &mut preview_record, &mut preview_candidate, &mut preview_root_supported,
                &mut diagnostic, preview)
        });
        let reader_progress = self.reader.progress();
        if reader_progress.diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
            self.reader_diagnostic = XmlDiagnostic { category: reader_progress.diagnostic.category,
                offset: reader_progress.diagnostic.offset };
        }
        if reader_status == ReaderStatus::Malformed {
            self.harvest_validation();
            self.publish_validated_preview();
            if !self.validation_complete { return IndexStatus::Ok; }
            self.diagnostic = if self.validation_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                self.validation_diagnostic
            } else if self.index_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None { self.index_diagnostic }
            else { self.reader_diagnostic };
            return IndexStatus::Malformed;
        }
        if reader_status == ReaderStatus::Complete {
            if self.depth != 0 || self.root_count != 1 {
                set_error(&mut self.index_diagnostic, XmlError::IncompleteDocument,
                    self.source_owner.len());
            } else { self.source_scanned = true; }
        }
        self.harvest_validation();
        self.publish_validated_preview();
        if self.validation_complete {
            if self.validation_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None
                && self.reader.progress().bytes_read >= self.validation_diagnostic.offset {
                self.diagnostic = self.validation_diagnostic;
                return IndexStatus::Malformed;
            }
            if self.index_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                self.diagnostic = if self.validation_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                    self.validation_diagnostic
                } else { self.index_diagnostic };
                return IndexStatus::Malformed;
            }
            if self.reader_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                self.diagnostic = if self.validation_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                    self.validation_diagnostic
                } else { self.reader_diagnostic };
                return IndexStatus::Malformed;
            }
        }
        if self.source_scanned && self.validation_complete { self.complete = true; }
        if self.complete { IndexStatus::Complete } else { IndexStatus::Ok }
    }

    pub fn progress(&self) -> IndexProgress {
        IndexProgress {
            bytes_read: self.reader.progress().bytes_read,
            source_bytes: self.source_owner.len(), element_count: self.elements.len(),
            attribute_count: self.attribute_count, token_count: self.token_count,
            generation: self.generation, diagnostic: self.diagnostic, complete: self.complete,
            canceled: self.canceled, first_preview_ready: self.preview,
        }
    }

    pub fn advance_generation(&mut self, generation: u64) -> IndexStatus {
        if generation <= self.generation { return IndexStatus::Invalid; }
        self.generation = generation;
        self.preview = false;
        self.preview_candidate = false;
        IndexStatus::Ok
    }

    pub fn preview_generation_is_current(&self, generation: u64) -> bool {
        !self.canceled && self.preview && generation == self.generation
    }

    pub fn cancel(&mut self) {
        if self.canceled { return; }
        self.canceled = true;
        let _ = self.queue.cancel(1);
    }

    pub fn element_at(&self, index: usize) -> Option<IndexElement> { self.elements.get(index).copied() }

    /// Token storage is visible only after full lexical and semantic completion.
    pub fn token_at(&self, index: usize) -> Option<XmlToken> {
        if self.complete { self.tokens.get(index).copied() } else { None }
    }

    pub fn make_preview_source(&self) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {
        if !self.preview || self.root_open_length == 0 || self.preview_record >= self.elements.len() {
            return None;
        }
        let source = self.source_owner.as_slice();
        let root = self.elements.first()?;
        let shape = self.elements.get(self.preview_record)?;
        if span_slice(source, XmlSpan { offset: root.name_offset, length: root.name_length })? != b"svg"
            || shape.source_length == 0 { return None; }
        let total = self.root_open_length.checked_add(shape.source_length)?.checked_add(6)?;
        if total > MAX_PREVIEW_SOURCE_BYTES { return None; }
        let mut output = Vec::new();
        output.try_reserve_exact(total).ok()?;
        output.extend_from_slice(source.get(root.source_offset..root.source_offset.checked_add(self.root_open_length)?)?);
        output.extend_from_slice(source.get(shape.source_offset..shape.source_offset.checked_add(shape.source_length)?)?);
        output.extend_from_slice(b"</svg>");
        Some(output)
    }

    fn harvest_validation(&mut self) {
        if self.validation_complete { return; }
        let Some(result) = self.queue.poll() else { return; };
        self.validation_complete = true;
        let mut guard = lock(&self.worker.result);
        if let Some(validated) = guard.take() {
            self.token_count = validated.tokens.len();
            self.tokens = validated.tokens;
            if validated.diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                self.validation_diagnostic = validated.diagnostic;
            } else if !result.succeeded {
                self.validation_diagnostic = XmlDiagnostic { category: XmlError::OutputExhausted, offset: 0 };
            } else if self.reader_diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
                self.validation_diagnostic = self.reader_diagnostic;
            }
        } else if !result.succeeded {
            self.validation_diagnostic = XmlDiagnostic { category: XmlError::OutputExhausted, offset: 0 };
        }
    }

    fn publish_validated_preview(&mut self) {
        if !self.preview_candidate || self.preview { return; }
        let Some(shape) = self.elements.get(self.preview_record) else { return; };
        let Some(end) = shape.source_offset.checked_add(shape.source_length) else { return; };
        let frontier = if self.worker.failed.load(Ordering::Acquire) {
            self.worker.error_offset.load(Ordering::Relaxed)
        } else { self.worker.frontier.load(Ordering::Acquire) };
        if frontier >= end { self.preview = true; }
    }
}

impl Drop for IndexSession<'_> {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        self.cancel();
        self.queue.shutdown();
    }
}

fn validate_document(context: &mut (Arc<WorkerState>, Arc<Vec<u8>>), token: vexel_platform_tasks::CancellationToken<'_>) -> TaskOutput {
    let (worker, source) = context;
    let mut stream = match XmlTokenStream::new_visitor(source.as_slice()) {
        Ok(stream) => stream,
        Err(_) => {
            *lock(&worker.result) = Some(ValidationResult {
                diagnostic: XmlDiagnostic { category: XmlError::OutputExhausted, offset: 0 },
                tokens: Vec::new(),
            });
            return TaskOutput::failure(XmlError::OutputExhausted as i64);
        }
    };
    let scratch = stream.visitor_storage_bytes();
    // XmlTokenStream also reserves its fixed MAX_DEPTH open-name vector.
    let parser_stack = MAX_DEPTH.saturating_mul(size_of::<XmlSpan>());
    let token_budget = MAX_COMPONENT_BYTES.saturating_sub(scratch).saturating_sub(parser_stack);
    let mut tokens: Vec<XmlToken> = Vec::new();
    let mut allocation_failed = false;
    let mut status = StreamStatus::Ok;
    while status == StreamStatus::Ok {
        status = stream.step_with_visitor_and_cancel(MAX_READER_STEP_BYTES,
            &mut |item| {
                if tokens.len() == tokens.capacity() {
                    let next = if tokens.capacity() == 0 { 64 } else {
                        match tokens.capacity().checked_mul(2) {
                            Some(value) => value,
                            None => { allocation_failed = true; return false; }
                        }
                    };
                    let Some(bytes) = next.checked_mul(size_of::<XmlToken>()) else {
                        allocation_failed = true; return false;
                    };
                    if bytes > token_budget || tokens.try_reserve_exact(next.saturating_sub(tokens.len())).is_err()
                        || tokens.capacity().checked_mul(size_of::<XmlToken>()).is_none_or(|actual| actual > token_budget) {
                        allocation_failed = true; return false;
                    }
                }
                tokens.push(*item);
                true
            },
            &mut || token.is_cancelled());
        worker.frontier.store(stream.bytes_read(), Ordering::Release);
        let partial = stream.result();
        if partial.diagnostic.category != XmlError::None {
            worker.error_offset.store(partial.diagnostic.offset, Ordering::Relaxed);
            worker.failed.store(true, Ordering::Release);
        }
        if token.is_cancelled() { break; }
    }
    if token.is_cancelled() || status == StreamStatus::Canceled {
        return TaskOutput::failure(XmlError::OutputExhausted as i64);
    }
    let mut diagnostic = stream.result().diagnostic;
    if allocation_failed {
        diagnostic = XmlDiagnostic { category: XmlError::OutputExhausted, offset: worker.frontier.load(Ordering::Acquire) };
    }
    let succeeded = status == StreamStatus::Complete && diagnostic.category == XmlError::None;
    if !succeeded { tokens = Vec::new(); }
    *lock(&worker.result) = Some(ValidationResult { diagnostic, tokens });
    if succeeded { TaskOutput::success(0) }
    else { TaskOutput::failure(diagnostic.category as i64) }
}

fn index_tag(source: &[u8], tag: ReaderTag, elements: &mut Vec<IndexElement>, element_storage: &mut usize,
    attribute_count: &mut usize, depth: &mut usize, stack: &mut [OpenElement; MAX_DEPTH], root_count: &mut usize,
    root_open_length: &mut usize, preview_record: &mut usize, preview_candidate: &mut bool,
    preview_root_supported: &mut bool, diagnostic: &mut XmlDiagnostic, preview: bool) -> bool {
    if diagnostic.category != XmlError::None { return true; }
    let closing = tag.kind == TagKind::EndElement;
    let self_closing = tag.kind == TagKind::EmptyElement;
    if tag.attribute_count > MAX_ATTRIBUTES.saturating_sub(*attribute_count) {
        set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::AttributeLimit, tag.source.start); return true;
    }
    *attribute_count += tag.attribute_count;
    if closing {
        if *depth == 0 { set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::MismatchedTag, tag.source.start); return true; }
        let top = stack[*depth - 1];
        if top.name.length != tag.name.end.saturating_sub(tag.name.start) || span_slice(source, top.name) != span_slice(source, reader_span(tag.name)) {
            set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::MismatchedTag, tag.source.start); return true;
        }
        *depth -= 1;
        if let Some(element) = elements.get_mut(top.record) {
            element.source_length = tag.source.end.saturating_sub(element.source_offset);
            element.closed = true;
            if !*preview_candidate && !preview && *depth == 1 && *preview_root_supported
                && element.support != ElementSupport::Unsupported {
                *preview_candidate = true; *preview_record = top.record;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
    if tag.name.end.saturating_sub(tag.name.start) == 0 || tag.name.end.saturating_sub(tag.name.start) == MAX_TOKEN_NAME_BYTES {
        set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::InvalidName, tag.name.start); return true;
    }
    if *depth >= MAX_DEPTH { set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::DepthLimit, tag.source.start); return true; }
    if *depth == 0 {
        *root_count += 1;
        if *root_count > 1 { set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::MultipleRoots, tag.source.start); return true; }
    }
    if elements.len() >= MAX_ELEMENTS { set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::NodeLimit, tag.source.start); return true; }
    if elements.len() == elements.capacity() {
        let next = if elements.capacity() == 0 { 256 } else { elements.capacity().saturating_mul(2) }.min(MAX_ELEMENTS);
        let Some(bytes) = next.checked_mul(size_of::<IndexElement>()) else {
            set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::NodeLimit, tag.source.start); return true;
        };
        if bytes > MAX_COMPONENT_BYTES.saturating_sub(*element_storage)
            || elements.try_reserve_exact(next.saturating_sub(elements.len())).is_err() {
            set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::NodeLimit, tag.source.start); return true;
        }
        *element_storage = size_of::<[OpenElement; MAX_DEPTH]>()
            .saturating_add(elements.capacity().saturating_mul(size_of::<IndexElement>()));
        if *element_storage > MAX_COMPONENT_BYTES { set_error(diagnostic, XmlError::NodeLimit, tag.source.start); return true; }
    }
    let name = reader_span(tag.name);
    let parent = if *depth == 0 { usize::MAX } else { stack[*depth - 1].record };
    let support = match span_slice(source, name) {
        Some(b"rect") => ElementSupport::Rect,
        Some(b"path") => ElementSupport::Path,
        _ => ElementSupport::Unsupported,
    };
    let index = elements.len();
    elements.push(IndexElement { parent, source_offset: tag.source.start,
        source_length: tag.source.end.saturating_sub(tag.source.start), name_offset: name.offset,
        name_length: name.length, depth: *depth, support, closed: self_closing });
    if *depth == 0 {
        *root_open_length = tag.source.end.saturating_sub(tag.source.start);
        *preview_root_supported = span_slice(source, name) == Some(b"svg")
            && preview_attributes_supported(source, tag, ElementSupport::Unsupported);
    }
    if *depth == 1 && elements[index].support != ElementSupport::Unsupported
        && !preview_attributes_supported(source, tag, elements[index].support) {
        elements[index].support = ElementSupport::Unsupported;
    }
    if !*preview_candidate && !preview && *depth == 1 && *preview_root_supported && self_closing
        && elements[index].support != ElementSupport::Unsupported {
        *preview_candidate = true; *preview_record = index;
    }
    if !self_closing {
        stack[*depth] = OpenElement { record: index, name };
        *depth += 1;
    }
    true
}

fn preview_attributes_supported(source: &[u8], tag: ReaderTag, shape: ElementSupport) -> bool {
    if tag.source.end.saturating_sub(tag.source.start) > MAX_STEP_BYTES { return false; }
    let Some(mut at) = tag.name.end.checked_add(0) else { return false; };
    let Some(end) = tag.source.end.checked_sub(0) else { return false; };
    let Some(bytes) = source.get(..end) else { return false; };
    let mut width = false;
    let mut height = false;
    let mut data = false;
    while at < end {
        while at < end && is_xml_space(bytes[at]) { at += 1; }
        if at >= end || matches!(bytes[at], b'>' | b'/') { break; }
        let name_start = at;
        while at < end && !is_xml_space(bytes[at]) && !matches!(bytes[at], b'=' | b'/' | b'>') { at += 1; }
        let name = &bytes[name_start..at];
        if name.is_empty() || name.contains(&b':') { return false; }
        while at < end && is_xml_space(bytes[at]) { at += 1; }
        if bytes.get(at) != Some(&b'=') { return false; }
        at += 1;
        while at < end && is_xml_space(bytes[at]) { at += 1; }
        let Some(&quote @ (b'\'' | b'"')) = bytes.get(at) else { return false; };
        at += 1;
        let value_start = at;
        while at < end && bytes[at] != quote { at += 1; }
        if at >= end { return false; }
        let value = &bytes[value_start..at];
        let accepted = match shape {
            ElementSupport::Unsupported => {
                if name == b"width" { width = true; }
                if name == b"height" { height = true; }
                if name == b"xmlns" && value != b"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" { return false; }
                matches!(name, b"xmlns" | b"version" | b"width" | b"height" | b"viewBox")
            }
            ElementSupport::Rect => {
                if name == b"width" { width = true; }
                if name == b"height" { height = true; }
                matches!(name, b"fill" | b"fill-rule" | b"x" | b"y" | b"width" | b"height")
            }
            ElementSupport::Path => {
                if name == b"d" { data = true; }
                matches!(name, b"fill" | b"fill-rule" | b"d")
            }
        };
        if !accepted { return false; }
        at += 1;
    }
    match shape {
        ElementSupport::Unsupported => width && height,
        ElementSupport::Rect => width && height,
        ElementSupport::Path => data,
    }
}

fn is_xml_space(byte: u8) -> bool { matches!(byte, b' ' | b'\t' | b'\r' | b'\n') }
fn span_slice(source: &[u8], span: XmlSpan) -> Option<&[u8]> { source.get(span.offset..span.offset.checked_add(span.length)?) }
fn reader_span(span: vexel_base::Span) -> XmlSpan { XmlSpan { offset: span.start, length: span.end.saturating_sub(span.start) } }
fn set_error(diagnostic: &mut XmlDiagnostic, category: XmlError, offset: usize) {
    if diagnostic.category == XmlError::None { *diagnostic = XmlDiagnostic { category, offset }; }
}
fn lock<T>(mutex: &Mutex<T>) -> MutexGuard<'_, T> { mutex.lock().unwrap_or_else(std::sync::PoisonError::into_inner) }
use std::sync::Arc;

use vexel_svg_index::{
    ElementSupport, IndexSession, IndexStatus, MAX_STEP_BYTES,
};
use vexel_xml::{tokenize, XmlDiagnostic, XmlError, XmlLimits};

fn source(bytes: &[u8]) -> Arc<Vec<u8>> { Arc::new(bytes.to_vec()) }

fn finish(session: &mut IndexSession<'_>, budget: usize) -> IndexStatus {
    for _ in 0..250_000 {
        let status = session.step(budget);
        if status != IndexStatus::Ok { return status; }
        std::thread::yield_now();
    }
    panic!("index did not finish within the bounded deterministic step loop")
}

#[test]
fn incremental_progress_preview_and_full_token_spans_match_the_xml_oracle() {
    let bytes = source(b"<svg width='2' height='2'><rect width='2' height='2'/><custom/><path d='M0 0'/></svg>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&bytes, 7).unwrap();
    let initial = session.progress();
    assert_eq!(initial.bytes_read, 0);
    assert_eq!(initial.generation, 7);
    assert_eq!(initial.token_count, 0);
    assert!(session.token_at(0).is_none());
    let first = session.step(1);
    assert_eq!(first, IndexStatus::Ok);
    assert!(session.progress().bytes_read <= 1);

    let mut saw_preview_before_complete = false;
    let mut previous = session.progress().bytes_read;
    let outcome = loop {
        let status = session.step(1);
        let progress = session.progress();
        assert!(progress.bytes_read >= previous);
        assert!(progress.bytes_read - previous <= 1);
        previous = progress.bytes_read;
        saw_preview_before_complete |= progress.first_preview_ready && !progress.complete;
        if status != IndexStatus::Ok { break status; }
    };
    assert_eq!(outcome, IndexStatus::Complete);
    let progress = session.progress();
    assert!(progress.complete);
    assert!(progress.first_preview_ready, "{progress:?}");
    assert!(saw_preview_before_complete);
    assert_eq!((progress.element_count, progress.attribute_count), (4, 5));

    let rect = session.element_at(1).unwrap();
    let rect_source = b"<rect width='2' height='2'/>";
    assert_eq!(rect.support, ElementSupport::Rect);
    assert_eq!(rect.depth, 1);
    assert_eq!(rect.parent, 0);
    assert!(rect.closed);
    assert_eq!(&bytes[rect.source_offset..rect.source_offset + rect.source_length], rect_source);
    assert_eq!(session.element_at(2).unwrap().support, ElementSupport::Unsupported);

    let preview = session.make_preview_source().unwrap();
    assert_eq!(preview, b"<svg width='2' height='2'><rect width='2' height='2'/></svg>");
    assert!(session.preview_generation_is_current(7));
    assert!(!session.preview_generation_is_current(8));

    let (expected, expected_result) = tokenize(bytes.as_slice(), XmlLimits::default());
    assert_eq!(expected_result.diagnostic, XmlDiagnostic::default());
    assert_eq!(progress.token_count, expected.len());
    for (index, token) in expected.iter().enumerate() {
        assert_eq!(session.token_at(index), Some(*token));
    }
}

#[test]
fn nested_element_parent_and_full_source_spans_are_retained() {
    let bytes = source(b"<svg width='2' height='2'><g><rect width='1' height='1'/></g></svg>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&bytes, 1).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, MAX_STEP_BYTES), IndexStatus::Complete);
    let root = session.element_at(0).unwrap();
    let group = session.element_at(1).unwrap();
    let child = session.element_at(2).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(root.parent, usize::MAX);
    assert_eq!(root.source_offset, 0);
    assert_eq!(root.source_length, bytes.len());
    assert!(root.closed);
    assert_eq!(group.parent, 0);
    assert_eq!(&bytes[group.source_offset..group.source_offset + group.source_length], b"<g><rect width='1' height='1'/></g>");
    assert!(group.closed);
    assert_eq!(child.parent, 1);
    assert_eq!(&bytes[child.source_offset..child.source_offset + child.source_length], b"<rect width='1' height='1'/>");
}

#[test]
fn doctype_and_rich_xml_keep_original_token_kinds_and_source_spans() {
    let doctype = source(b"<?xml version='1.0'?>\n<!DOCTYPE svg PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD SVG 1.1//EN\" \"x.dtd\" [\n<!-- ]> \">\" --><!ENTITY e \"a>b]\">\n]>\n<svg><rect/></svg>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&doctype, 1).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, 5), IndexStatus::Complete);
    assert_eq!(session.progress().element_count, 2);

    let rich = source(b"<?xml version='1.0' encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\r\n<!--c--><?p data?><a:root xmlns:a='urn:x' a:k=\"v&amp;x\">x\r\ny<![CDATA[z]]><a:child/></a:root>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&rich, 3).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, 3), IndexStatus::Complete);
    let (expected, result) = tokenize(rich.as_slice(), XmlLimits::default());
    assert_eq!(result.diagnostic, XmlDiagnostic::default());
    assert_eq!(session.progress().token_count, expected.len());
    for (index, token) in expected.iter().enumerate() {
        assert_eq!(session.token_at(index), Some(*token));
    }
}

#[test]
fn malformed_prefix_blocks_preview_and_malformed_tail_preserves_valid_preview() {
    let prefix = source(b"<svg width='2' height='2'>bad & raw<rect width='2' height='2'/></svg>");
    let prefix_offset = prefix.iter().position(|byte| *byte == b'&').unwrap();
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&prefix, 2).unwrap();
    let mut preview_ever_published = false;
    let status = loop {
        let status = session.step(1);
        preview_ever_published |= session.progress().first_preview_ready;
        if status != IndexStatus::Ok { break status; }
        std::thread::yield_now();
    };
    assert_eq!(status, IndexStatus::Malformed);
    assert!(!preview_ever_published);
    assert_eq!(session.progress().diagnostic, XmlDiagnostic { category: XmlError::MalformedSyntax, offset: prefix_offset });

    let tail = source(b"<svg width='2' height='2'><rect width='1' height='1'/></broken>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&tail, 3).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, 3), IndexStatus::Malformed);
    let progress = session.progress();
    assert!(progress.first_preview_ready, "{progress:?}");
    assert!(!progress.complete);
    assert_eq!(progress.diagnostic, XmlDiagnostic {
        category: XmlError::MismatchedTag,
        offset: tail.windows(b"</broken>".len()).position(|part| part == b"</broken>").unwrap(),
    });
    assert_eq!(progress.diagnostic, tokenize(tail.as_slice(), XmlLimits::default()).1.diagnostic);
}

#[test]
fn exact_diagnostics_unsupported_gate_generation_invalidation_and_cancellation() {
    for source_bytes in [
        &b"<svg><rect/></bad>"[..],
        &b"<svg><rect width=1/></svg>"[..],
        &b"<svg><!-- -- --></svg>"[..],
        &b"<!ENTITY e \"x\"><svg/>"[..],
        &b"<svg><rect x='1' x='2'/></svg>"[..],
        &b"<svg><rect"[..],
    ] {
        let bytes = source(source_bytes);
        let mut session = IndexSession::start(&bytes, 1).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, 3), IndexStatus::Malformed);
        assert_eq!(session.progress().diagnostic, tokenize(source_bytes, XmlLimits::default()).1.diagnostic);
    }

    let unsupported = source(b"<svg width='2' height='2'><rect width='1' height='1' transform='translate(1)'/><rect width='1' height='1'/></svg>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&unsupported, 4).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, MAX_STEP_BYTES), IndexStatus::Complete);
    assert_eq!(session.element_at(1).unwrap().support, ElementSupport::Unsupported);
    assert_eq!(session.element_at(2).unwrap().support, ElementSupport::Rect);
    assert_eq!(session.make_preview_source().unwrap(), b"<svg width='2' height='2'><rect width='1' height='1'/></svg>");
    assert_eq!(session.advance_generation(3), IndexStatus::Invalid);
    assert_eq!(session.advance_generation(5), IndexStatus::Ok);
    assert!(!session.progress().first_preview_ready);
    assert!(!session.preview_generation_is_current(4));
    assert!(!session.preview_generation_is_current(5));

    let path = source(b"<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='2' height='2'><path fill='red' d='M0 0'/></svg>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&path, 2).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, MAX_STEP_BYTES), IndexStatus::Complete);
    assert_eq!(session.element_at(1).unwrap().support, ElementSupport::Path);
    assert_eq!(session.make_preview_source().unwrap(), path.as_slice());

    let non_svg = source(b"<g><rect width='2' height='2'/></g>");
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&non_svg, 4).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, MAX_STEP_BYTES), IndexStatus::Complete);
    assert!(!session.progress().first_preview_ready);
    assert!(session.make_preview_source().is_none());

    for target_percent in [10, 50, 90] {
        let mut data = vec![b' '; 1024 * 1024];
        let prefix = b"<svg><rect width='1' height='1'/>";
        let suffix = b"</svg>";
        data[..prefix.len()].copy_from_slice(prefix);
        let tail_start = data.len() - suffix.len();
        data[tail_start..].copy_from_slice(suffix);
        let bytes = Arc::new(data);
        let mut canceled = IndexSession::start(&bytes, 6).unwrap();
        let mut progress = canceled.progress();
        while progress.bytes_read.saturating_mul(100) / progress.source_bytes < target_percent {
            assert_eq!(canceled.step(MAX_STEP_BYTES), IndexStatus::Ok);
            progress = canceled.progress();
        }
        assert!(!progress.complete);
        canceled.cancel();
        assert_eq!(canceled.step(64), IndexStatus::Canceled);
        assert!(canceled.progress().canceled);
        drop(canceled); // joins the validator before the borrowed source can be released
    }
}

#[test]
fn large_start_tag_is_indexed_without_becoming_preview_eligible() {
    let mut bytes = Vec::new();
    let prefix = b"<svg width='";
    let suffix = b"' height='1'><rect width='1' height='1'/></svg>";
    let target = 128 * 1024;
    bytes.extend_from_slice(prefix);
    bytes.resize(target - suffix.len(), b'1');
    bytes.extend_from_slice(suffix);
    let bytes = Arc::new(bytes);
    let mut session = IndexSession::start(&bytes, 9).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(finish(&mut session, MAX_STEP_BYTES), IndexStatus::Complete);
    assert!(!session.progress().first_preview_ready);
    assert!(session.element_at(1).is_some());
}
